<newsitem itemid="624618" id="root" date="1997-05-29" xml:lang="en">
<title>NETHERLANDS: ING Q1 net profit NLG 891 mln.</title>
<headline>ING Q1 net profit NLG 891 mln.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>First quarter 1997</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)		   1.19  vs    1.04</p>
<p>    Net profit				    891  vs  736</p>
<p>    Pre-tax insurance profit		  651  vs  568</p>
<p>    Pre-tax banking profit		    620  vs  490</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had expected ING Groep NV to report a first quarter net profit of between 850 million and 946 million guilders.  </p>
<p>    Dividend on preference shrs (guilders) 11  vs   11</p>
<p>    Net attributable profit		880     vs  725</p>
<p>    Total income (billion)		  13.86  vs   11.52</p>
<p>    Total expenses (billion )	     12.59  vs   10.46</p>
<p>    Total pre-tax profit (billion)	 1.27  vs    1.06</p>
<p>    Total assets (billion)		 528.48  vs  424.20</p>
<p>    Shareholders equity (billions)	39.85  vs   26.2</p>
<p>Note - Earnings per share for 1996 have been restated to reflect a 2.5-for-one share split in June last year. Total asset and shareholders equity figures for 1996 are as at March 31.  </p>
<p>    Tax					  346     vs  306</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
